# Milestone: M5
# Covers: at (cond) body onleave cleanup — onleave fires on falling edge after
#         body has fired on rising edge; BODY_FIRED_SINCE_ONLEAVE guard prevents
#         onleave without a preceding body fire.
#
# defer-to: M5-scratch-frame
#
# Reason:
#   invoke_onleave_inline is a M5-stub (uwatcher_eval.c); it is a no-op unless
#   test_watcher_onleave_hook is set.  The at_with_onleave_fires_on_falling_edge
#   unit test (test_at_fire_paths.c T43) exercises this via hook.  The RAII
#   cleanup pattern requires scratch-frame execution to run onleave closures.
#
# Activate when scratch-frame execution is wired.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at M5 scratch-frame):
#   var x = 0;
#   var log = "";
#   at (x > 5) Realm.log = Realm.log + "up" onleave Realm.log = Realm.log + "down";
#   Realm.x = 10;
#   Realm.x = 0;
#   log
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000000] 0
#   [00000001] ""
#   [00000002] nil
#   [00000003] 10
#   [00000004] 0
#   [00000005] "updown"
